// frost map file — painted cells on a tile grid.
// tilesets: the tileset documents this map's layers cut from, by
// path relative to THIS file. Each layer names its tileset by the
// name that document speaks. Cells stand as named records — (x, y)
// counted from the layer's top-left, tile: the cell's number in the
// cut, and tfm: the tile's turn, written only when it is turned.
// An absent cell is empty, and empty cells are not written.
//
// The courtyard: twelve by eight. The floor layer wears the slab
// (tile 0) inside; the rampart layer wears the half-wedge (tile 1)
// all round the perimeter — thirty-six cells, the boxes the lamp's
// shadows sweep by. No cell wears both offices.
